    "task_outcome_detailed": "This screening task evaluated 23 candidate studies (indices 70-92) against the review     
protocol for 'Menopausal status, ultrasound and biomarker tests in combination for the diagnosis of ovarian cancer in   
symptomatic women'. The selection criteria required: (1) cross-sectional diagnostic test accuracy studies evaluating    
single tests or comparing two or more tests, (2) randomised trials comparing two or more tests, or (3) studies          
validating multivariable models for OC diagnosis investigating test combinations, with reference standard of            
histological confirmation or clinical follow-up in women with pelvic mass suspicious for OC.\n\nINCLUDED STUDIES (9):\n-
Study 71: Diagnostic study of 129 patients with pelvic masses evaluating HE4, CA-125, and ROMA combination\n- Study 72: 
Prospective study of 50 women with complex pelvic masses evaluating HE4, CA125, ROMA, and RMI\n- Study 74: Study of 104 
women with pelvic mass evaluating ROMA with histological reference standard\n- Study 77: Population-based study of 901  
women with pelvic masses evaluating RMI, ROMA, CA125, and HE4\n- Study 80: Multicenter study of 2445 patients evaluating
IOTA models, IOTA simple rules, and RMI\n- Study 81: Subset analysis of 229 premenopausal patients evaluating HE4 and   
CA-125\n- Study 89: Diagnostic performance study of 832 patients evaluating CA125, HE4, and ROMA\n- Study 91:           
Multicenter clinical trial of 638 women evaluating HE4, CA125, ROMA, and RMI\n- Study 92: Study of 353 patients         
evaluating ADNEX model vs subjective assessment\n\nEXCLUDED STUDIES (14):\n- Systematic reviews/meta-analyses (6):      
Studies 70, 79, 86, 88, plus reviews that synthesize rather than generate primary data\n- Methodology papers (3):       
Studies 73 (PROBAST tool), 76 (bivariate analysis methods), 78 (MetaDAS SAS macro)\n- Wrong cancer/outcome (4): Study 75
(routes to diagnosis across all cancers), Study 82 (prognosis/therapy monitoring), Study 83 (benign disorders only),    
Study 87 (endometrial cancer)\n- Review articles (1): Study 84 (biomarkers review)\n- Method development (1): Study 85  
(HE4 ELISA assay development)\n\nThe included studies provide primary diagnostic accuracy data on biomarker combinations
(HE4, CA125, ROMA) and ultrasound-based multivariable models (IOTA, ADNEX, RMI) in the target population of women with  
pelvic masses suspicious for ovarian cancer.",                                                                          
    "additional_context": "Key screening decisions were based on strict adherence to the protocol requiring primary     
diagnostic accuracy studies. Systematic reviews and meta-analyses were excluded as they are secondary syntheses rather  
than primary evidence. Studies focusing on prognosis, therapy monitoring, or benign disorders were excluded as they do  
not address the diagnostic accuracy question for women with suspicious pelvic masses. The 9 included studies            
collectively cover biomarker combinations and multivariable models across diverse populations including pre- and        
postmenopausal women, with reference standards of histological confirmation."                                           
